NUM-15: reject a FUNCTIONAL storage exponent of -1 or less

A FUNCTIONAL storage unit's volume is the integral of A0 + A1*Depth^A2 from
depth 0, which storage_getVolume() evaluates as A0*d + A1/(A2+1)*d^(A2+1).
The integral does not exist for A2 <= -1: at -1 the code divides by zero
and every volume is inf (continuity error NaN), below -1 it returns a finite
number for an infinite integral. storage_readParams() only checked A0.
Reject A2 <= -1 with ERROR 211 (invalid number) at the exponent token, as a
negative A0 already is.
The 6.0.0 check sits in the [STORAGE] handler.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-15_swmm600.patch

